[?2004l[?2004h> This review weighs every line in the draft letter against the client's recorded messages, following the protocol that the clarification prevails where it speaks and the original instruction governs only where the clarification leaves the subject alone. The per-line table names the governing entry for each line, and results.json carries the four totals. The finding is that the draft cannot be sent as written: lines are verified only where they take the full position of the governing entry, while lines are at odds where they reverse the position, omit a required limb, or identify a different person. Some lines are not in the record at all because neither message addresses their subject, and a nonexistent citation never determined that outcome by itself. This record-based review therefore holds the letter until each line has been checked against what the client actually said first and second.
